{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794533976274,"sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","part":{"partID":"prt_1d28f6788001YaaM33l4JhEh6D","sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","messageID":"msg_1d28f5a5f001vR7XjBDfMq7Ffm","type":"tool","id":"call_913501ff2a5d42c792f4561b","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt"},"output":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt, lines 1-203\n1: # /doctor:skill-advisor Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>`: startup questions, the route manifest display, setup prompts, the rebuild plan and approval, diagnostic dashboards, result templates, troubleshooting, and next-step text. The command router owns target resolution and asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Startup Presentation\n6: \n7: When `$ARGUMENTS` lacks a recognized positional target, ask this prompt first after reading `_routes.yaml`.\n8: \n9: ```text\n10: What do you want to do with the skill advisor?\n11: \n12:    1) Re-tune routing                    (which skill gets recommended)\n13:    2) Rebuild the skill graph            (skill-graph.sqlite from graph-metadata.json)\n14:    3) Check skill-graph freshness        (compiled vs sqlite vs disk drift)\n15:    4) Check router reach                 (declared phrases reach their hub)\n16:    5) Audit description budget           (char counts, CI-friendly)\n17:    6) Audit parent-skill structure       (mode registry, graph metadata)\n18:    H) Help me decide\n19:    X) Cancel\n20: ```\n21: \n22: Accepted answers:\n23: \n24: | Answer | Result |\n25: |--------|--------|\n26: | `1` | target = `tune` |\n27: | `2` | target = `rebuild` |\n28: | `3` | target = `skill-graph-freshness` |\n29: | `4` | target = `router-reach` |\n30: | `5` | target = `skill-budget` |\n31: | `6` | target = `parent-skill` |\n32: | `H` | Show the help block, then ask the startup prompt again |\n33: | `X`, empty, `cancel` | `STATUS=CANCEL` |\n34: \n35: On any other response, re-emit the menu once. On a second invalid response, return `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=unknown_selection`.\n36: \n37: ### Help Block\n38: \n39: ```text\n40: Pick by symptom:\n41: \n42:    Advisor recommends the wrong skill                  -> 1  Re-tune routing\n43:    New skill not appearing in advisor results          -> 2  Rebuild, then 3 to confirm\n44:    advisor_status reports stale, absent or unavailable -> 2  Rebuild\n45:    Compiled/sqlite/disk skill-graph disagree           -> 3  Skill-graph freshness\n46:    Declared router phrase reaches the wrong hub        -> 4  Router reach\n47:    Description char-count over hard cap                -> 5  Description budget\n48:    Parent skill graph-metadata or mode registry drift  -> 6  Parent-skill structure\n49: \n50: Quick reference for confusable pairs:\n51:    Re-tune (1) edits scoring lanes after per-skill review; Rebuild (2) only re-derives the graph\n52:    Freshness (3) reports drift; Rebuild (2) repairs it\n53:    Description budget (5) audits CHAR COUNTS, not routing quality\n54: \n55: Press 1-6, H, or X.\n56: ```\n57: \n58: ### Unknown Target Failure\n59: \n60: ```text\n61: Unknown target: [target]\n62: Valid targets: tune, rebuild, skill-graph-freshness, router-reach, skill-budget, parent-skill\n63: Try: /doctor:skill-advisor list\n64: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_target\"\n65: ```\n66: \n67: ### Cross-Target Flag Failure\n68: \n69: ```text\n70: Flag '[flag]' is not valid for target '[target]'. Did you mean `/doctor:skill-advisor [suggested-target] [flag]`?\n71: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"cross_target_flag_injection\"\n72: ```\n73: \n74: ## 2. Route Manifest Display\n75: \n76: Render this table for `list`, `?`, or `--list`. Values should mirror `_routes.yaml`.\n77: \n78: | Target | Workflow | Mutation Class | One-Line Purpose |\n79: |--------|----------|----------------|------------------|\n80: | `tune` | `doctor-skill-advisor-tune.yaml` | mutates | Audit and re-tune the advisor's scoring lanes, with per-skill review before any write |\n81: | `rebuild` | `doctor-skill-advisor-rebuild.yaml` | mutates | Rebuild skill-graph.sqlite from graph-metadata.json through the advisor CLI, behind a backup |\n82: | `skill-graph-freshness` | `doctor-skill-graph-freshness.yaml` | read-only | Diagnose skill-graph representation drift across compiled, sqlite, and disk sources |\n83: | `router-reach` | `doctor-router-reach.yaml` | read-only | Ask the live advisor whether every phrase a hub's router advertises actually reaches it |\n84: | `skill-budget` | `doctor-skill-budget.yaml` | read-only | Audit skill, command, and agent description budgets |\n85: | `parent-skill` | `doctor-parent-skill.yaml` | read-only | Audit parent-skill structure, routing manifests, root metadata, router contract, and version consistency |\n86: \n87: ## 3. Setup Prompts\n88: \n89: Ask only prompts needed for unresolved setup variables. Do not split a required setup question into multiple visible turns.\n90: \n91: ### Tune Scope\n92: \n93: Ask only when `--scope` was not passed.\n94: \n95: ```text\n96: Which scoring lanes should be checked?\n97:    1) all       - explicit, derived, and lexical\n98:    2) explicit  - TOKEN_BOOSTS and PHRASE_BOOSTS\n99:    3) derived   - graph-metadata triggers and topics\n100:    4) lexical   - CATEGORY_HINTS\n101: ```\n102: \n103: Accept `1-4` or the corresponding name; empty defaults to `all`.\n104: \n105: ### Parent-Skill Directory\n106: \n107: Ask only when `--dir` was not passed: `Which parent skill hub should be audited? (path under .skilled/skills/)`. The fleet-wide metadata gate runs either way.\n108: \n109: ### Router-Reach Scope\n110: \n111: `--hub` and `--concurrency` are optional. With neither, the whole fleet is probed at the script's default concurrency; ask nothing.\n112: \n113: ## 4. Rebuild Plan And Approval\n114: \n115: Render the plan after the probe, before any write.\n116: \n117: ```text\n118: SKILL GRAPH REBUILD PLAN\n119: Advisor status: [live|stale|absent|unavailable] (daemon: [running|absent])\n120: Database: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite ([size], modified [time] | not present)\n121: Backup: [backup path | none, no database yet]\n122: Source: [N] graph-metadata.json files under .skilled/skills/\n123: Will run:\n124:    node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_rebuild --trusted --force true\n125:    node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted\n126: ```\n127: \n128: With `--dry-run`, follow the plan with `Dry run: nothing was written.` and `STATUS=OK`.\n129: \n130: Otherwise ask:\n131: \n132: ```text\n133: Rebuild the skill graph now? The current database is backed up first and restored if the rebuild fails.\n134: Reply approve to rebuild, or no to cancel.\n135: ```\n136: \n137: ## 5. Setup Dashboard\n138: \n139: Render this compact panel after setup and before YAML execution when target resolution or flags were non-trivial.\n140: \n141: ```text\n142: DOCTOR ROUTE SETUP\n143: Target: [target]\n144: Workflow: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/[yaml]\n145: Mutation class: [read-only|mutates]\n146: Execution mode: INTERACTIVE\n147: Setup values: [key=value list]\n148: Presentation: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\n149: Next: load workflow YAML\n150: ```\n151: \n152: ## 6. Result Templates\n153: \n154: Use the target workflow output contract when it provides a stricter report shape. Use these templates for summary display and fallback rendering.\n155: \n156: ### Read-Only Diagnostic Summary\n157: \n158: ```text\n159: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n160: Target: [target]\n161: Workflow: [yaml]\n162: Status: [OK|DEGRADED|ATTENTION|CANCELLED|FAIL|ERROR]\n163: Mutation class: read-only\n164: Evidence: [checks, counts, failing rows, or report path]\n165: Recommendation: [operator action or none]\n166: STATUS=[status]\n167: ```\n168: \n169: ### Mutating Target Summary\n170: \n171: ```text\n172: DOCTOR MUTATING RESULT\n173: Target: [target]\n174: Workflow: [yaml]\n175: Status: [OK|CANCELLED|FAIL|ROLLED_BACK]\n176: Approved changes: [none|summary]\n177: Files modified: [list or none]\n178: Verification: [checks run and result]\n179: Rollback: [backup path or not required]\n180: STATUS=[status]\n181: ```\n182: \n183: ### Failure Summary\n184: \n185: ```text\n186: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n187: Target: [target]\n188: Step: [setup|workflow phase]\n189: Error: [message]\n190: Next: [recommended command or manual action]\n191: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[message]\"\n192: ```\n193: \n194: ## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n195: \n196: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n197: |-----------|------------------|\n198: | Advisor CLI exits 75 | The daemon is not running; a warm-only probe never starts it. `rebuild` does not need it |\n199: | Rebuild failed and was rolled back | Read the failing command's output, fix the named graph-metadata.json, rerun `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n200: | Cross-target flag rejected | Use the suggested target from the error |\n201: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n202: \n203: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt, lines 1-203\n1: # /doctor:skill-advisor Presentation Contract\n2: \n3: This file is the single source of truth for user-facing presentation in `/doctor:skill-advisor <target>`: startup questions, the route manifest display, setup prompts, the rebuild plan and approval, diagnostic dashboards, result templates, troubleshooting, and next-step text. The command router owns target resolution and asset routing only. The workflow YAML owns execution behavior.\n4: \n5: ## 1. Startup Presentation\n6: \n7: When `$ARGUMENTS` lacks a recognized positional target, ask this prompt first after reading `_routes.yaml`.\n8: \n9: ```text\n10: What do you want to do with the skill advisor?\n11: \n12:    1) Re-tune routing                    (which skill gets recommended)\n13:    2) Rebuild the skill graph            (skill-graph.sqlite from graph-metadata.json)\n14:    3) Check skill-graph freshness        (compiled vs sqlite vs disk drift)\n15:    4) Check router reach                 (declared phrases reach their hub)\n16:    5) Audit description budget           (char counts, CI-friendly)\n17:    6) Audit parent-skill structure       (mode registry, graph metadata)\n18:    H) Help me decide\n19:    X) Cancel\n20: ```\n21: \n22: Accepted answers:\n23: \n24: | Answer | Result |\n25: |--------|--------|\n26: | `1` | target = `tune` |\n27: | `2` | target = `rebuild` |\n28: | `3` | target = `skill-graph-freshness` |\n29: | `4` | target = `router-reach` |\n30: | `5` | target = `skill-budget` |\n31: | `6` | target = `parent-skill` |\n32: | `H` | Show the help block, then ask the startup prompt again |\n33: | `X`, empty, `cancel` | `STATUS=CANCEL` |\n34: \n35: On any other response, re-emit the menu once. On a second invalid response, return `STATUS=FAIL ERROR=unknown_selection`.\n36: \n37: ### Help Block\n38: \n39: ```text\n40: Pick by symptom:\n41: \n42:    Advisor recommends the wrong skill                  -> 1  Re-tune routing\n43:    New skill not appearing in advisor results          -> 2  Rebuild, then 3 to confirm\n44:    advisor_status reports stale, absent or unavailable -> 2  Rebuild\n45:    Compiled/sqlite/disk skill-graph disagree           -> 3  Skill-graph freshness\n46:    Declared router phrase reaches the wrong hub        -> 4  Router reach\n47:    Description char-count over hard cap                -> 5  Description budget\n48:    Parent skill graph-metadata or mode registry drift  -> 6  Parent-skill structure\n49: \n50: Quick reference for confusable pairs:\n51:    Re-tune (1) edits scoring lanes after per-skill review; Rebuild (2) only re-derives the graph\n52:    Freshness (3) reports drift; Rebuild (2) repairs it\n53:    Description budget (5) audits CHAR COUNTS, not routing quality\n54: \n55: Press 1-6, H, or X.\n56: ```\n57: \n58: ### Unknown Target Failure\n59: \n60: ```text\n61: Unknown target: [target]\n62: Valid targets: tune, rebuild, skill-graph-freshness, router-reach, skill-budget, parent-skill\n63: Try: /doctor:skill-advisor list\n64: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"unknown_target\"\n65: ```\n66: \n67: ### Cross-Target Flag Failure\n68: \n69: ```text\n70: Flag '[flag]' is not valid for target '[target]'. Did you mean `/doctor:skill-advisor [suggested-target] [flag]`?\n71: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"cross_target_flag_injection\"\n72: ```\n73: \n74: ## 2. Route Manifest Display\n75: \n76: Render this table for `list`, `?`, or `--list`. Values should mirror `_routes.yaml`.\n77: \n78: | Target | Workflow | Mutation Class | One-Line Purpose |\n79: |--------|----------|----------------|------------------|\n80: | `tune` | `doctor-skill-advisor-tune.yaml` | mutates | Audit and re-tune the advisor's scoring lanes, with per-skill review before any write |\n81: | `rebuild` | `doctor-skill-advisor-rebuild.yaml` | mutates | Rebuild skill-graph.sqlite from graph-metadata.json through the advisor CLI, behind a backup |\n82: | `skill-graph-freshness` | `doctor-skill-graph-freshness.yaml` | read-only | Diagnose skill-graph representation drift across compiled, sqlite, and disk sources |\n83: | `router-reach` | `doctor-router-reach.yaml` | read-only | Ask the live advisor whether every phrase a hub's router advertises actually reaches it |\n84: | `skill-budget` | `doctor-skill-budget.yaml` | read-only | Audit skill, command, and agent description budgets |\n85: | `parent-skill` | `doctor-parent-skill.yaml` | read-only | Audit parent-skill structure, routing manifests, root metadata, router contract, and version consistency |\n86: \n87: ## 3. Setup Prompts\n88: \n89: Ask only prompts needed for unresolved setup variables. Do not split a required setup question into multiple visible turns.\n90: \n91: ### Tune Scope\n92: \n93: Ask only when `--scope` was not passed.\n94: \n95: ```text\n96: Which scoring lanes should be checked?\n97:    1) all       - explicit, derived, and lexical\n98:    2) explicit  - TOKEN_BOOSTS and PHRASE_BOOSTS\n99:    3) derived   - graph-metadata triggers and topics\n100:    4) lexical   - CATEGORY_HINTS\n101: ```\n102: \n103: Accept `1-4` or the corresponding name; empty defaults to `all`.\n104: \n105: ### Parent-Skill Directory\n106: \n107: Ask only when `--dir` was not passed: `Which parent skill hub should be audited? (path under .skilled/skills/)`. The fleet-wide metadata gate runs either way.\n108: \n109: ### Router-Reach Scope\n110: \n111: `--hub` and `--concurrency` are optional. With neither, the whole fleet is probed at the script's default concurrency; ask nothing.\n112: \n113: ## 4. Rebuild Plan And Approval\n114: \n115: Render the plan after the probe, before any write.\n116: \n117: ```text\n118: SKILL GRAPH REBUILD PLAN\n119: Advisor status: [live|stale|absent|unavailable] (daemon: [running|absent])\n120: Database: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite ([size], modified [time] | not present)\n121: Backup: [backup path | none, no database yet]\n122: Source: [N] graph-metadata.json files under .skilled/skills/\n123: Will run:\n124:    node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_rebuild --trusted --force true\n125:    node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs skill_graph_scan --trusted\n126: ```\n127: \n128: With `--dry-run`, follow the plan with `Dry run: nothing was written.` and `STATUS=OK`.\n129: \n130: Otherwise ask:\n131: \n132: ```text\n133: Rebuild the skill graph now? The current database is backed up first and restored if the rebuild fails.\n134: Reply approve to rebuild, or no to cancel.\n135: ```\n136: \n137: ## 5. Setup Dashboard\n138: \n139: Render this compact panel after setup and before YAML execution when target resolution or flags were non-trivial.\n140: \n141: ```text\n142: DOCTOR ROUTE SETUP\n143: Target: [target]\n144: Workflow: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/[yaml]\n145: Mutation class: [read-only|mutates]\n146: Execution mode: INTERACTIVE\n147: Setup values: [key=value list]\n148: Presentation: .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\n149: Next: load workflow YAML\n150: ```\n151: \n152: ## 6. Result Templates\n153: \n154: Use the target workflow output contract when it provides a stricter report shape. Use these templates for summary display and fallback rendering.\n155: \n156: ### Read-Only Diagnostic Summary\n157: \n158: ```text\n159: DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT\n160: Target: [target]\n161: Workflow: [yaml]\n162: Status: [OK|DEGRADED|ATTENTION|CANCELLED|FAIL|ERROR]\n163: Mutation class: read-only\n164: Evidence: [checks, counts, failing rows, or report path]\n165: Recommendation: [operator action or none]\n166: STATUS=[status]\n167: ```\n168: \n169: ### Mutating Target Summary\n170: \n171: ```text\n172: DOCTOR MUTATING RESULT\n173: Target: [target]\n174: Workflow: [yaml]\n175: Status: [OK|CANCELLED|FAIL|ROLLED_BACK]\n176: Approved changes: [none|summary]\n177: Files modified: [list or none]\n178: Verification: [checks run and result]\n179: Rollback: [backup path or not required]\n180: STATUS=[status]\n181: ```\n182: \n183: ### Failure Summary\n184: \n185: ```text\n186: DOCTOR TARGET FAILED\n187: Target: [target]\n188: Step: [setup|workflow phase]\n189: Error: [message]\n190: Next: [recommended command or manual action]\n191: STATUS=FAIL ERROR=\"[message]\"\n192: ```\n193: \n194: ## 7. Troubleshooting Display\n195: \n196: | Situation | Suggested Action |\n197: |-----------|------------------|\n198: | Advisor CLI exits 75 | The daemon is not running; a warm-only probe never starts it. `rebuild` does not need it |\n199: | Rebuild failed and was rolled back | Read the failing command's output, fix the named graph-metadata.json, rerun `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild` |\n200: | Cross-target flag rejected | Use the suggested target from the error |\n201: | Route manifest parse error | Run `bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh` |\n202: \n203: End interactive presentations with: `What would you like to do next?`"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1794533975944,"end":1794533976274}}}}
