{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794534228511,"sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2933fc70026iWw6ieb7wsfTu","sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","messageID":"msg_1d2932ae6001dREo7gNVFHzZ5r","type":"tool","id":"call_5c8bc62daece429ba5a54fc2","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n -i \"restart the (advisor )?daemon|daemon restart\" .skilled --glob '!**/dist/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' | head -20"},"output":".skilled/bin/hf-model-server.cjs:51:// fixed value so idle daemon restarts stay just as fast.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/SKILL.md:98:- **Daemon**: local HTTP server on `127.0.0.1:3456` (not a socket), auth via `X-Daemon-Token` at `~/.figma-ds-cli/.daemon-token`, PID `~/.figma-cli-daemon.pid`, idle ~60 min, not reboot-persistent. Verbs: `daemon status | diagnose | start | stop | restart | reconnect`. \"Unauthorized\" → `daemon diagnose` then `daemon restart` (never auto-delete the token).\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/examples/README.md:123:| `daemon status` unreachable | Daemon idle-stopped (~60 min) or never started | `figma-ds-cli daemon diagnose`, then `daemon restart` |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/examples/safe-connect-daemon-health.sh:78:  fail \"recovery path per SKILL.md: daemon diagnose, then daemon restart.\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/README.md:79:The status verb reports healthy or points at the problem. \"Unauthorized\" means run `daemon diagnose`, then `daemon restart`. Never delete or paste the token at `~/.figma-ds-cli/.daemon-token`.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/README.md:153:| `Unauthorized` from a daemon command | The daemon token is stale or the daemon is unhealthy | Run `figma-ds-cli daemon diagnose`, then `daemon restart`. Never auto-delete the token at `~/.figma-ds-cli/.daemon-token` |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/figma-cli-reference.md:140:figma-ds-cli daemon restart            # restart + regenerate token    (mutating)\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/figma-cli-reference.md:144:All illustrative; verify with `figma-ds-cli daemon --help`. A token mismatch surfaces as \"Unauthorized: Invalid or missing token\", so run `daemon diagnose` then `daemon restart` (never auto-delete the token). **[CONFIRMED: `REFERENCE.md`]**\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/tool-surface.md:79:| Daemon | `daemon restart` | MUTATING | Restarts daemon, regenerates token. App-level. |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/troubleshooting.md:340:figma-ds-cli daemon restart 2>&1    # restart re-aligns the token\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/troubleshooting.md:365:1. **Idle / crashed**: `figma-ds-cli daemon restart` (then `daemon reconnect` if the bridge is up but the document link dropped).\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/troubleshooting.md:366:2. **Port owned by another process**: identify the owner with `lsof` first, and **never blind-kill** the port. If it is a stale figma-ds-cli daemon, `daemon restart`, but otherwise resolve the owning process before reusing 3456.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/troubleshooting.md:443:| Daemon `Unauthorized` | `X-Daemon-Token` mismatch | `daemon diagnose` then `daemon restart` (never delete token) |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/troubleshooting.md:444:| Daemon unreachable on 3456 | Idle timeout / crash / port owned | `daemon restart`/`reconnect`; identify 3456 owner before reuse |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:274:❌ **STOP if validation fails.** Review [Troubleshooting](#9-troubleshooting), confirm Figma Desktop is open with a file, then restart the daemon.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:131:The lane weights live in `runtime/lib/scorer/lane-registry.ts`. The scorer reads `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON`. The launcher allowlist passes it through to the daemon child. An env change needs a daemon restart to apply. Use the env variable for experiments. Durable tuning is editing `lane-registry.ts` with measured evidence. Run `advisor_validate` before and after the change. Ship the diff with doc updates across the feature catalog and the advisor scorer reference.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:232:A: Yes, with measured evidence. `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON` is allowlisted through the launcher for experiments (daemon restart required). The durable path is a source edit in `runtime/lib/scorer/lane-registry.ts`: run `advisor_validate` to capture a baseline, change the weights, re-run validate, ship the diff with doc updates in `references/scoring/advisor-scorer.md` and the feature catalog.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/scoring/lane-weight-tuning.md:91:- It requires a daemon restart to apply and suits short-lived experiments only.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/runtime/freshness-contract.md:156:| Daemon dies | `advisor_status.daemon = \"down\"`, trustState may stay `live` until next file change but freshness detection lags | Restart the daemon (the next CLI call cold-starts it) |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/runtime/freshness-contract.md:159:| File watcher overflow (too many files) | Daemon stops detecting changes | Restart the daemon. Long-term: prune `.skilled/skills/` excludes |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/bin/hf-model-server.cjs:51:// fixed value so idle daemon restarts stay just as fast.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/SKILL.md:98:- **Daemon**: local HTTP server on `127.0.0.1:3456` (not a socket), auth via `X-Daemon-Token` at `~/.figma-ds-cli/.daemon-token`, PID `~/.figma-cli-daemon.pid`, idle ~60 min, not reboot-persistent. Verbs: `daemon status | diagnose | start | stop | restart | reconnect`. \"Unauthorized\" → `daemon diagnose` then `daemon restart` (never auto-delete the token).\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/examples/README.md:123:| `daemon status` unreachable | Daemon idle-stopped (~60 min) or never started | `figma-ds-cli daemon diagnose`, then `daemon restart` |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/examples/safe-connect-daemon-health.sh:78:  fail \"recovery path per SKILL.md: daemon diagnose, then daemon restart.\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/README.md:79:The status verb reports healthy or points at the problem. \"Unauthorized\" means run `daemon diagnose`, then `daemon restart`. Never delete or paste the token at `~/.figma-ds-cli/.daemon-token`.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/README.md:153:| `Unauthorized` from a daemon command | The daemon token is stale or the daemon is unhealthy | Run `figma-ds-cli daemon diagnose`, then `daemon restart`. Never auto-delete the token at `~/.figma-ds-cli/.daemon-token` |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/figma-cli-reference.md:140:figma-ds-cli daemon restart            # restart + regenerate token    (mutating)\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/figma-cli-reference.md:144:All illustrative; verify with `figma-ds-cli daemon --help`. A token mismatch surfaces as \"Unauthorized: Invalid or missing token\", so run `daemon diagnose` then `daemon restart` (never auto-delete the token). **[CONFIRMED: `REFERENCE.md`]**\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/tool-surface.md:79:| Daemon | `daemon restart` | MUTATING | Restarts daemon, regenerates token. App-level. |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/troubleshooting.md:340:figma-ds-cli daemon restart 2>&1    # restart re-aligns the token\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/troubleshooting.md:365:1. **Idle / crashed**: `figma-ds-cli daemon restart` (then `daemon reconnect` if the bridge is up but the document link dropped).\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/troubleshooting.md:366:2. **Port owned by another process**: identify the owner with `lsof` first, and **never blind-kill** the port. If it is a stale figma-ds-cli daemon, `daemon restart`, but otherwise resolve the owning process before reusing 3456.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/troubleshooting.md:443:| Daemon `Unauthorized` | `X-Daemon-Token` mismatch | `daemon diagnose` then `daemon restart` (never delete token) |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/troubleshooting.md:444:| Daemon unreachable on 3456 | Idle timeout / crash / port owned | `daemon restart`/`reconnect`; identify 3456 owner before reuse |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:274:❌ **STOP if validation fails.** Review [Troubleshooting](#9-troubleshooting), confirm Figma Desktop is open with a file, then restart the daemon.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:131:The lane weights live in `runtime/lib/scorer/lane-registry.ts`. The scorer reads `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON`. The launcher allowlist passes it through to the daemon child. An env change needs a daemon restart to apply. Use the env variable for experiments. Durable tuning is editing `lane-registry.ts` with measured evidence. Run `advisor_validate` before and after the change. Ship the diff with doc updates across the feature catalog and the advisor scorer reference.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:232:A: Yes, with measured evidence. `SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON` is allowlisted through the launcher for experiments (daemon restart required). The durable path is a source edit in `runtime/lib/scorer/lane-registry.ts`: run `advisor_validate` to capture a baseline, change the weights, re-run validate, ship the diff with doc updates in `references/scoring/advisor-scorer.md` and the feature catalog.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/scoring/lane-weight-tuning.md:91:- It requires a daemon restart to apply and suits short-lived experiments only.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/runtime/freshness-contract.md:156:| Daemon dies | `advisor_status.daemon = \"down\"`, trustState may stay `live` until next file change but freshness detection lags | Restart the daemon (the next CLI call cold-starts it) |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/references/runtime/freshness-contract.md:159:| File watcher overflow (too many files) | Daemon stops detecting changes | Restart the daemon. Long-term: prune `.skilled/skills/` excludes |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n -i \\\"restart the (advisor )?daemon|daemon restart\\\" .skilled --glob '!**/dist/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794534227911,"end":1794534228511}}}}
