{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794534238574,"sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","part":{"id":"prt_1d293696e001cy6he42h5n602Q","sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","messageID":"msg_1d2935f3a001gAkQdS5LL5Irsv","type":"step-start","snapshot":"fc0e8b3933380d56852b3e8d92ff212ee815b5b6"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794534247623,"sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2938a8500131QPEAl5YUvUwZ","sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","messageID":"msg_1d2935f3a001gAkQdS5LL5Irsv","type":"tool","id":"call_1bddc25157c94ab384244384","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n -i \"embed|ollama|nomic\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md | head -30; echo ---; rg -n -i \"embed|ollama|nomic\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md | head -20"},"output":"274:## 12. CHOOSING AN EMBEDDER\n276:The skill-advisor `semantic_shadow` lane runs against a pluggable embedder layer. As of phase `003/006` the contract surface (adapter interface, types, manifest registry, Ollama adapter) lives in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor now owns. Skill-advisor's local `runtime/lib/embedders/` files are thin re-export shims plus a skill-advisor-specific `schema.ts` integration that targets the package-local SQLite database at `runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite`. This section is the new-user onboarding view; the canonical embedder narrative lives at [embedder-pluggability.md](../system-spec-kit/references/memory/embedder-pluggability.md).\n280:The persisted default is the `'auto'` sentinel. On daemon startup, `ensureActiveEmbedder()` invokes the shared cascade and persists the winner to `vec_metadata`. The cascade probes (in order):\n284:| 1 | Ollama running with a known text manifest pulled | `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` (first match in priority list) |\n285:| 2 | hf-local model server reachable (pure-Node `@huggingface/transformers` HTTP client, zero Python) | `nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5` (hf-local) |\n286:| 3 | `OPENAI_API_KEY` present | `text-embedding-3-small` (1536-dim) |\n289:If every probe fails the daemon logs a warning and `semantic_shadow` scoring may degrade. The cascade only fires when the persisted pointer is `'auto'` or references a manifest the shared registry no longer knows about (legacy `embeddinggemma-300m` from a pre-phase-007 install). Manual `setActiveEmbedder()` calls take precedence — they pin the pointer and the cascade skips on subsequent restarts.\n291:Phase `002/jina-swap-and-reindex` runbook plus phase `004/skill-graph-db-writer-cross-wire` together make the swap safe end-to-end. The writer dispatcher (`refreshSkillEmbeddings()`) routes through `refreshSkillEmbeddingsViaAdapter` when an active pointer is set and falls back to the legacy `createEmbeddingsProvider` factory only when the cascade has not yet resolved (e.g. cold start before any probe succeeds).\n295:Source of truth: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/registry.ts`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/registry.ts). Skill-advisor's local `runtime/lib/embedders/registry.ts` is a re-export shim — adding manifests is a single edit in the shared package. The seven text-tuned manifests registered today, each as a frozen `EmbedderManifest`:\n297:| Name | Dim | Backend | Ollama tag | Max input | Notes |\n299:| `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` | 768 | `ollama` | `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 5000 | 768-dim retrieval specialist. Local-first cascade default per ADR-014. Uses `search_query: ` / `search_document: ` prefix tokens. |\n300:| `mxbai-embed-large-v1` | 1024 | `ollama` | `mxbai-embed-large:latest` | 1200 | Phase `016/004` paraphrase-strong candidate. |\n301:| `bge-small-en-v1.5` | 384 | `ollama` | `bge-small-en-v1.5:latest` | n/a | Compact 33M-param baseline. |\n302:| `bge-large-en-v1.5` | 1024 | `ollama` | `bge-large-en-v1.5:latest` | n/a | BAAI flagship retrieval model. |\n303:| `jina-embeddings-v3` | 1024 | `ollama` | `hf.co/gaianet/jina-embeddings-v3-GGUF:Q4_K_M` | 8000 | Multilingual + paraphrase-tuned. Matryoshka representation allows 256 / 512 / 768 / 1024 truncation. |\n304:| `bge-m3` | 1024 | `ollama` | `bge-m3:latest` | 8000 | Multilingual hybrid (dense + sparse + colbert). |\n305:| `snowflake-arctic-embed-l-v2.0` | 1024 | `ollama` | `snowflake-arctic-embed2:latest` | 8000 | Snowflake late-2024 flagship. 8192 context, multilingual, top MTEB retrieval scores. |\n307:> **Content-type split.** The TS shared registry is text-tuned by design. The `contentType: 'text' \\| 'code'` parameter on the shared cascade preserves the conceptual split for any future TS code consumer. The previous skill-advisor-specific `jina-embeddings-v2-base-code` entry was removed because it was code-tuned and did not belong in a text-only registry.\n309:Adding a new candidate is a single registry row in the shared package plus, if the backend is new, a single adapter under `shared/embeddings/adapters/`. No call sites change. The adapter contract (`EmbedderAdapter` in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/adapter.ts`) is small — `embed()` plus `ready()`.\n311:### 12.3 Swap mechanism: `'auto'` sentinel + `setActiveEmbedder()`\n315:**Sentinel-driven (default).** `vec_metadata` starts unpopulated; `getActiveEmbedder()` returns `{ name: 'auto', dim: 0 }`. The first daemon start invokes `ensureActiveEmbedder()` which calls the shared cascade and persists the winner. Subsequent daemon starts read the persisted pointer and skip the cascade.\n317:**Manual override.** [`setActiveEmbedder()`](./runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts) writes a specific manifest into `vec_metadata` and creates the matching `vec_<dim>` table:\n321:import { setActiveEmbedder } from './runtime/dist/.../lib/embedders/schema.js';\n324:setActiveEmbedder(db, 'jina-embeddings-v3', 1024);\n329:- `vec_metadata.active_embedder_name` -> `jina-embeddings-v3`\n330:- `vec_metadata.active_embedder_dim` -> `1024`\n331:- `vec_1024` table created (if absent), schema `(skill_id, embedding BLOB, model_id, content_hash, updated_at)`\n332:- `hasActiveEmbedderPointer(db)` returns `true`, so both read path (`semantic-shadow.ts`, `loadSkillEmbeddings()`) and write path (`refreshSkillEmbeddingsViaAdapter`) target `vec_<active.dim>`\n335:There are intentionally no embedder-administration commands here. Skill-advisor's surface is one database helper plus the cascade-driven sentinel. Operator discipline owns any manual swap workflow; there is no async re-index orchestrator on the skill-advisor side.\n343:3. (Optional) Call `setActiveEmbedder()` to override the cascade choice.\n---\n106:4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n119:| 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"274:## 12. CHOOSING AN EMBEDDER\n276:The skill-advisor `semantic_shadow` lane runs against a pluggable embedder layer. As of phase `003/006` the contract surface (adapter interface, types, manifest registry, Ollama adapter) lives in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/`, which the advisor now owns. Skill-advisor's local `runtime/lib/embedders/` files are thin re-export shims plus a skill-advisor-specific `schema.ts` integration that targets the package-local SQLite database at `runtime/database/skill-graph.sqlite`. This section is the new-user onboarding view; the canonical embedder narrative lives at [embedder-pluggability.md](../system-spec-kit/references/memory/embedder-pluggability.md).\n280:The persisted default is the `'auto'` sentinel. On daemon startup, `ensureActiveEmbedder()` invokes the shared cascade and persists the winner to `vec_metadata`. The cascade probes (in order):\n284:| 1 | Ollama running with a known text manifest pulled | `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` (first match in priority list) |\n285:| 2 | hf-local model server reachable (pure-Node `@huggingface/transformers` HTTP client, zero Python) | `nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5` (hf-local) |\n286:| 3 | `OPENAI_API_KEY` present | `text-embedding-3-small` (1536-dim) |\n289:If every probe fails the daemon logs a warning and `semantic_shadow` scoring may degrade. The cascade only fires when the persisted pointer is `'auto'` or references a manifest the shared registry no longer knows about (legacy `embeddinggemma-300m` from a pre-phase-007 install). Manual `setActiveEmbedder()` calls take precedence — they pin the pointer and the cascade skips on subsequent restarts.\n291:Phase `002/jina-swap-and-reindex` runbook plus phase `004/skill-graph-db-writer-cross-wire` together make the swap safe end-to-end. The writer dispatcher (`refreshSkillEmbeddings()`) routes through `refreshSkillEmbeddingsViaAdapter` when an active pointer is set and falls back to the legacy `createEmbeddingsProvider` factory only when the cascade has not yet resolved (e.g. cold start before any probe succeeds).\n295:Source of truth: [`@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/registry.ts`](../system-spec-kit/shared/embeddings/registry.ts). Skill-advisor's local `runtime/lib/embedders/registry.ts` is a re-export shim — adding manifests is a single edit in the shared package. The seven text-tuned manifests registered today, each as a frozen `EmbedderManifest`:\n297:| Name | Dim | Backend | Ollama tag | Max input | Notes |\n299:| `nomic-embed-text-v1.5` | 768 | `ollama` | `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 5000 | 768-dim retrieval specialist. Local-first cascade default per ADR-014. Uses `search_query: ` / `search_document: ` prefix tokens. |\n300:| `mxbai-embed-large-v1` | 1024 | `ollama` | `mxbai-embed-large:latest` | 1200 | Phase `016/004` paraphrase-strong candidate. |\n301:| `bge-small-en-v1.5` | 384 | `ollama` | `bge-small-en-v1.5:latest` | n/a | Compact 33M-param baseline. |\n302:| `bge-large-en-v1.5` | 1024 | `ollama` | `bge-large-en-v1.5:latest` | n/a | BAAI flagship retrieval model. |\n303:| `jina-embeddings-v3` | 1024 | `ollama` | `hf.co/gaianet/jina-embeddings-v3-GGUF:Q4_K_M` | 8000 | Multilingual + paraphrase-tuned. Matryoshka representation allows 256 / 512 / 768 / 1024 truncation. |\n304:| `bge-m3` | 1024 | `ollama` | `bge-m3:latest` | 8000 | Multilingual hybrid (dense + sparse + colbert). |\n305:| `snowflake-arctic-embed-l-v2.0` | 1024 | `ollama` | `snowflake-arctic-embed2:latest` | 8000 | Snowflake late-2024 flagship. 8192 context, multilingual, top MTEB retrieval scores. |\n307:> **Content-type split.** The TS shared registry is text-tuned by design. The `contentType: 'text' \\| 'code'` parameter on the shared cascade preserves the conceptual split for any future TS code consumer. The previous skill-advisor-specific `jina-embeddings-v2-base-code` entry was removed because it was code-tuned and did not belong in a text-only registry.\n309:Adding a new candidate is a single registry row in the shared package plus, if the backend is new, a single adapter under `shared/embeddings/adapters/`. No call sites change. The adapter contract (`EmbedderAdapter` in `@spec-kit/shared/embeddings/adapter.ts`) is small — `embed()` plus `ready()`.\n311:### 12.3 Swap mechanism: `'auto'` sentinel + `setActiveEmbedder()`\n315:**Sentinel-driven (default).** `vec_metadata` starts unpopulated; `getActiveEmbedder()` returns `{ name: 'auto', dim: 0 }`. The first daemon start invokes `ensureActiveEmbedder()` which calls the shared cascade and persists the winner. Subsequent daemon starts read the persisted pointer and skip the cascade.\n317:**Manual override.** [`setActiveEmbedder()`](./runtime/lib/embedders/schema.ts) writes a specific manifest into `vec_metadata` and creates the matching `vec_<dim>` table:\n321:import { setActiveEmbedder } from './runtime/dist/.../lib/embedders/schema.js';\n324:setActiveEmbedder(db, 'jina-embeddings-v3', 1024);\n329:- `vec_metadata.active_embedder_name` -> `jina-embeddings-v3`\n330:- `vec_metadata.active_embedder_dim` -> `1024`\n331:- `vec_1024` table created (if absent), schema `(skill_id, embedding BLOB, model_id, content_hash, updated_at)`\n332:- `hasActiveEmbedderPointer(db)` returns `true`, so both read path (`semantic-shadow.ts`, `loadSkillEmbeddings()`) and write path (`refreshSkillEmbeddingsViaAdapter`) target `vec_<active.dim>`\n335:There are intentionally no embedder-administration commands here. Skill-advisor's surface is one database helper plus the cascade-driven sentinel. Operator discipline owns any manual swap workflow; there is no async re-index orchestrator on the skill-advisor side.\n343:3. (Optional) Call `setActiveEmbedder()` to override the cascade choice.\n---\n106:4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n119:| 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n -i \\\"embed|ollama|nomic\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/INSTALL-GUIDE.md | head -30; echo ---; rg -n -i \\\"embed|ollama|nomic\\\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794534247045,"end":1794534247623}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794534248957,"sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","part":{"id":"prt_1d29391fd001d8d9x2L3Oq6wfN","sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","messageID":"msg_1d2935f3a001gAkQdS5LL5Irsv","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"03ec5e035580729e15868e6338fd56f3aafe7ae0","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":683,"output":102,"reasoning":906,"cache":{"read":71552,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794534253085,"sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","part":{"id":"prt_1d293a21d001vvAvdoY5mUTIKq","sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","messageID":"msg_1d2939202001RS77zk64VtYmZz","type":"step-start","snapshot":"3b3f6d1e0b523911e597f258318b862da9d07f39"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794534256889,"sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","part":{"partID":"prt_1d293af3c001Ua37eGah3aqgWB","sessionID":"ses_e2d72f595ffeUyzS41y9fhQRh9","messageID":"msg_1d2939202001RS77zk64VtYmZz","type":"tool","id":"call_3df9f351f569425aa4a9f4ce","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '115,140p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-rebuild.yaml; echo ===; sed -n '1,60p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-setup.yaml"},"output":"# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OUTPUT\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noutput:\n  presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"\n  statuses: [OK, CANCELLED, ROLLED_BACK, FAIL]\n===\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DOCTOR: SK-GIT SETUP BATTERY (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Diagnostic Operator reporting whether the sk-git setup passes its read-only battery end to end\npurpose: Run the read-only battery over the sk-git install, hooks, trust, gates, standards, allowlist, worktrees, Commit-Id policy, advisory rules, suppressors and AI-tool hook registration, and name the repair command for each failing check\naction: Run .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs once -> render its per-check PASS/FAIL/SKIP/UNKNOWN/DEGRADED verdict and repair lines through the presentation contract\nskill_owner: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPERATING MODE\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: single-step\n  compliance: MANDATORY\n  execution: read_only\n  approvals: none\n  tracking: single_run\n  validation: read_only_assertion\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nmutation_boundaries:\n  read_only: true\n  allowed_targets: []\n  forbidden_targets:\n    - \"**/*\"\n  invariant: \"Every check runs in its check-only form and the battery prints a repair command instead of applying one. This route MUST NOT install hooks, set trust, write git config or .sk-git/, request a Commit-Id or provision a worktree. Repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of a diagnostic.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# UPSTREAM ASSETS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nupstream_assets:\n  setup_battery: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# INPUTS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ninputs:\n  target: \"setup is one of the route's three targets, along with hooks and standards: /doctor:git setup runs it. Any other positional fails before this YAML loads.\"\n  tool: \"--tool=<name> names the AI tool running the check: claude, codex, devin, cursor, opencode, pi or dsh. A DSH run is judged by its repo-guards bundle: the adapter link .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/git-preflight-advisory.mjs must resolve, the bundle entry must import and call its register function, and the real adapter must register tools/post-execute and import git-rule-checks.mjs. For other tools, that tool's adapter must register the advisory under its own pre-tool event for its shell tool, and an OpenCode or Pi adapter must register its event handler and import git-rule-checks.mjs. Every other adapter is checked the same way and fails only when its file exists without the registration. Without --tool, and outside Claude Code, the row is UNKNOWN and names --tool.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# EXECUTION\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nexecution:\n  steps:\n    - \"Run .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs once. Add --tool=<name> when the AI tool executing this command is claude, codex, devin, cursor, opencode, pi or dsh. On any other runtime, run it without --tool, because the battery accepts no other name.\"\n    - \"The battery runs eleven checks in order: install (the toolchain is present), hooks (every shipped hook is installed, resolves to this repository's or this checkout's hook source and is executable), trust (passes for this checkout, a repository with local skilled.trustRepoHooks=true or hooks linked into its own tree, otherwise SKIP), gates (the saved hook gate settings, where a gate saved off is DEGRADED), standards (the contract folder and the rule copies in force), allowlist (the remote-branch allowlist patterns), worktrees (the worktree base and the provisioning entries, DEGRADED when the base sits inside the main checkout with more than three linked worktrees, plus an informational fsmonitor daemons line counting main, worktree and stray daemons from a dry run of .skilled/bin/fsmonitor-daemon-reaper.sh that never changes the verdict, and an informational numbered worktrees line counting what a dry run of .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh --numbered would reap, keep and report as orphan folders, which never changes the verdict either), commit-id (the Commit-Id policy helper decides whether the repository wants ids and checks that the allocator ships when they are wanted), advisory-rules (reads the inspected repository's .skilled/skills/sk-git/hard-rules.json, fails when the file is not a JSON array or names an unknown check and is DEGRADED when missing), suppression (fails when a master switch is on and is DEGRADED when the advisory's own switches mute it), and ai-tool-hooks (every configured AI-tool adapter, and the named tool's, registers the git-preflight advisory for its shell tool).\"\n    - \"Each check prints one PASS|FAIL|SKIP|UNKNOWN|DEGRADED line with its source, its detail lines, and a repair: <command> line under each failure and each degraded row. The battery's last line is STATUS=OK checks=11, STATUS=DEGRADED degraded=<n> skipped=<n> unknown=<n>, or STATUS=FAIL failed=<n> degraded=<n> skipped=<n> unknown=<n>.\"\n    - \"Render the battery's verdict through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-presentation.txt: the per-check table and the DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT summary, with the repair command under each failure.\"\n    - \"Map the battery's exit code to the route status: 0 every check passes or skips, 3 degraded (no check failed, but at least one check is UNKNOWN or DEGRADED), 1 any failure, 2 bad argument or crash.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OUTPUT\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noutput: |\n  STATUS=OK when the battery exits 0 and its last line is STATUS=OK checks=11.\n  STATUS=DEGRADED when the battery exits 3 and its last line starts STATUS=DEGRADED. This means no check failed and at least one check is UNKNOWN or DEGRADED. List each UNKNOWN or DEGRADED check with its detail lines and include any repair command its repair: line printed.\n  STATUS=FAIL when the battery exits 1. List each failing check with the repair command its repair: line printed, and each degraded, skipped or unknown check.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OUTPUT\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noutput:\n  presentation: \".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-presentation.txt\"\n  statuses: [OK, CANCELLED, ROLLED_BACK, FAIL]\n===\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DOCTOR: SK-GIT SETUP BATTERY (READ-ONLY DIAGNOSTIC)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Diagnostic Operator reporting whether the sk-git setup passes its read-only battery end to end\npurpose: Run the read-only battery over the sk-git install, hooks, trust, gates, standards, allowlist, worktrees, Commit-Id policy, advisory rules, suppressors and AI-tool hook registration, and name the repair command for each failing check\naction: Run .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs once -> render its per-check PASS/FAIL/SKIP/UNKNOWN/DEGRADED verdict and repair lines through the presentation contract\nskill_owner: \".skilled/skills/sk-git/\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPERATING MODE\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: single-step\n  compliance: MANDATORY\n  execution: read_only\n  approvals: none\n  tracking: single_run\n  validation: read_only_assertion\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# MUTATION BOUNDARIES (READ-ONLY)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nmutation_boundaries:\n  read_only: true\n  allowed_targets: []\n  forbidden_targets:\n    - \"**/*\"\n  invariant: \"Every check runs in its check-only form and the battery prints a repair command instead of applying one. This route MUST NOT install hooks, set trust, write git config or .sk-git/, request a Commit-Id or provision a worktree. Repair is an explicit operator action, never a side effect of a diagnostic.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# UPSTREAM ASSETS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nupstream_assets:\n  setup_battery: \".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# INPUTS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ninputs:\n  target: \"setup is one of the route's three targets, along with hooks and standards: /doctor:git setup runs it. Any other positional fails before this YAML loads.\"\n  tool: \"--tool=<name> names the AI tool running the check: claude, codex, devin, cursor, opencode, pi or dsh. A DSH run is judged by its repo-guards bundle: the adapter link .dsh/plugins/repo-guards/adapters/git-preflight-advisory.mjs must resolve, the bundle entry must import and call its register function, and the real adapter must register tools/post-execute and import git-rule-checks.mjs. For other tools, that tool's adapter must register the advisory under its own pre-tool event for its shell tool, and an OpenCode or Pi adapter must register its event handler and import git-rule-checks.mjs. Every other adapter is checked the same way and fails only when its file exists without the registration. Without --tool, and outside Claude Code, the row is UNKNOWN and names --tool.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# EXECUTION\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nexecution:\n  steps:\n    - \"Run .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/git-setup-check.cjs once. Add --tool=<name> when the AI tool executing this command is claude, codex, devin, cursor, opencode, pi or dsh. On any other runtime, run it without --tool, because the battery accepts no other name.\"\n    - \"The battery runs eleven checks in order: install (the toolchain is present), hooks (every shipped hook is installed, resolves to this repository's or this checkout's hook source and is executable), trust (passes for this checkout, a repository with local skilled.trustRepoHooks=true or hooks linked into its own tree, otherwise SKIP), gates (the saved hook gate settings, where a gate saved off is DEGRADED), standards (the contract folder and the rule copies in force), allowlist (the remote-branch allowlist patterns), worktrees (the worktree base and the provisioning entries, DEGRADED when the base sits inside the main checkout with more than three linked worktrees, plus an informational fsmonitor daemons line counting main, worktree and stray daemons from a dry run of .skilled/bin/fsmonitor-daemon-reaper.sh that never changes the verdict, and an informational numbered worktrees line counting what a dry run of .skilled/bin/worktree-reaper.sh --numbered would reap, keep and report as orphan folders, which never changes the verdict either), commit-id (the Commit-Id policy helper decides whether the repository wants ids and checks that the allocator ships when they are wanted), advisory-rules (reads the inspected repository's .skilled/skills/sk-git/hard-rules.json, fails when the file is not a JSON array or names an unknown check and is DEGRADED when missing), suppression (fails when a master switch is on and is DEGRADED when the advisory's own switches mute it), and ai-tool-hooks (every configured AI-tool adapter, and the named tool's, registers the git-preflight advisory for its shell tool).\"\n    - \"Each check prints one PASS|FAIL|SKIP|UNKNOWN|DEGRADED line with its source, its detail lines, and a repair: <command> line under each failure and each degraded row. The battery's last line is STATUS=OK checks=11, STATUS=DEGRADED degraded=<n> skipped=<n> unknown=<n>, or STATUS=FAIL failed=<n> degraded=<n> skipped=<n> unknown=<n>.\"\n    - \"Render the battery's verdict through .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-presentation.txt: the per-check table and the DOCTOR DIAGNOSTIC RESULT summary, with the repair command under each failure.\"\n    - \"Map the battery's exit code to the route status: 0 every check passes or skips, 3 degraded (no check failed, but at least one check is UNKNOWN or DEGRADED), 1 any failure, 2 bad argument or crash.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OUTPUT\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noutput: |\n  STATUS=OK when the battery exits 0 and its last line is STATUS=OK checks=11.\n  STATUS=DEGRADED when the battery exits 3 and its last line starts STATUS=DEGRADED. This means no check failed and at least one check is UNKNOWN or DEGRADED. List each UNKNOWN or DEGRADED check with its detail lines and include any repair command its repair: line printed.\n  STATUS=FAIL when the battery exits 1. List each failing check with the repair command its repair: line printed, and each degraded, skipped or unknown check.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"sed -n '115,140p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-rebuild.yaml; echo ===; sed -n '1,60p' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-setup.yaml\"}"},"time":{"start":1794534256444,"end":1794534256889}}}}
